@startuml seq_com_alive_counter
title SC-COM-02 - Alive counter frozen or jumped

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-COM-003, SYS-COM-002, SYS-FLT-002, SIM-PLT-001, SIM-CON-001, SIM-CON-003, SG-04
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
AliveCtr: 4 bits, +1 (mod 16) per transmission (can_matrix section 3).
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal; example message SIM_Speed (0x101)
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 5
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 6
TCU -> TCU : +1: accepted

alt counter frozen
  User -> Console : freeze the alive counter of SIM_Speed (SIM-CON-003)
  Console -> Plant : freeze AliveCtr
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 6
  TCU -> TCU : counter did not change: message ignored (1)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 6
  TCU -> TCU : ignored (2)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 6
  TCU -> TCU : ignored (3): 3 consecutive ignored messages are treated\nas a timeout (SYS-COM-003)
  TCU -> TCU : communication fault SIM_Speed (FaultBits 8), substitute values,\nlimp-home (SYS-COM-002, SYS-FLT-002), see SC-COM-01
else counter jumped by more than 2
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 10
  TCU -> TCU : jump of 4 > 2: message ignored (SYS-COM-003)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 11
  TCU -> TCU : +1 compared with the last received message (10, ignored or not):\naccepted (SYS-COM-003)
else counter +1 or +2 (one frame lost)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: AliveCtr = 8
  TCU -> TCU : jump of 2: accepted
end

note over Plant, TCU
The TCU increments the AliveCtr of TCU_Actuators and TCU_Status by 1 per transmission (SYS-COM-003);
the console shows alive counter errors (SIM-CON-001).
end note
@enduml
